WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
TIKTOK BAN:
The United States wants to ban TikTok.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:08.580
They say that TikTok is Chinese spyware designed&nbsp;
to intrude on the privacy and lives of Americans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:15.060
and there is some truth to this. I mean, TikTok&nbsp;
doesn’t even try to hide it. If you go onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:20.400
their privacy policy page, they clearly list out&nbsp;
exactly what they collect. They of course collect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.580
the classic stuff like what device you’re using,&nbsp;
your IP address, and your location. But they also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.620
collect so more sus items like your biometrics&nbsp;
including your faceprint and voiceprint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.620
and that’s just the things that they admit to.&nbsp;
Who knows what other data the CC, I mean TikTok,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.300
may be collecting and what exactly they’re&nbsp;
doing with this data. To be honest though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.420
TikTok’s data collection is not all that different&nbsp;
from Facebook’s or Google’s or even Apple’s but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.120
since they’re a Chinese company, countries have&nbsp;
been much more cautious. In fact, several notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:00.660
countries have already banned the app like India&nbsp;
who banned it nearly 3 years ago. The US has also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.520
started taking action. Earlier this year, dozens&nbsp;
of college campuses banned the use of TikTok&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:12.060
on school Wifi. TikTok has also been banned on&nbsp;
government devices and its CEO has been grilled in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.040
Congress. But likely the scariest part for TikTok&nbsp;
is the fact that both sides of the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:22.260
are uniting on this issue. Some democrats have&nbsp;
even gone as far as admitting that Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:28.920
was right about TikTok the entire time. That’s&nbsp;
when you know you’re really screwed. But, if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.680
thought that TikTok was gonna lay down and take&nbsp;
this beating, you’d be mistaken. 3 years ago, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.540
ban was not something that they were anticipating,&nbsp;
meaning that they had to do as the US said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:45.180
including selling themselves to Oracle. But, this&nbsp;
time, they’ve had plenty of time to prepare and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.700
it looks like they already have an extensive three&nbsp;
phase plan in place. They’re currently working on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.920
the 3rd phase of this plan which is by far the&nbsp;
most evil as they’re essentially buying out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:02.280
bunch of Americans. So, join me as we explore&nbsp;
TikTok’s sneaky plan to avoid getting banned.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.420
PHASE 1 - STRIKE THE TENT:&nbsp;

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:15.540
Coming out on top on any deal is quite easy.&nbsp;
The key is to have leverage. 3 years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:21.060
America had all the leverage as it was TikTok that&nbsp;
was dependent on America. They were dependent on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:26.520
American creators, American viewers, and most&nbsp;
importantly, American consumerism and addiction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.460
These things are still very much true which&nbsp;
gives the US government quite a bit of power. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:38.820
the key for TikTok is to overcome this dependency&nbsp;
and the easiest way to do that is to ensure that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:44.940
the US is even more dependent on TikTok. The first&nbsp;
step in making this the reality was addressing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:51.420
American economy by launching TikTok ads in June&nbsp;
of 2020. To be honest, the usage of TikTok ads is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.780
still quite low. Most brands just don’t want to&nbsp;
get involved with short form cringe content. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:03.120
a lot of dropshippers and ecommerce gurus have&nbsp;
apparently made it work leading to a decent amount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:09.180
of revenue. In fact, TikTok is expected to pull&nbsp;
in $8.75 billion worth of revenue this year and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:14.940
$11 billion worth or revenue next year just from&nbsp;
the US. But wait a minute, doesn’t this just make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:21.540
TikTok even more dependent on the US? Well, that’s&nbsp;
how it appears at first glance but it’s not really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.660
true. For one, TikTok’s parent company, ByteDance,&nbsp;
pulled in $80 billion worth of revenue last year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:35.700
so the revenue from TikTok US is only about&nbsp;
10%. Still, 10% is not a bad amount right? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:41.940
that is until you consider that ByteDance&nbsp;
actually lost $7 billion running TikTok. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:47.160
financially speaking, ByteDance will be just fine&nbsp;
without TikTok; in fact, they’ll be better off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:53.220
This isn’t to say that ByteDance wants to lose&nbsp;
TikTok but they’re by no means dependent on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:59.220
revenue. Do you know who is dependent on TikTok&nbsp;
though? Creators and advertisers who built their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:04.860
businesses around the platform. So, it’s not&nbsp;
America who’s making TikTok a viable business.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:10.260
It’s actually ByteDance who’s subsidizing American&nbsp;
creators and advertisers. Think about this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:17.400
Every minute, people consume 167 million hours of&nbsp;
TikTok. Assuming that the average TikTok is viewed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:23.940
for 15 seconds, we’re talking about 668 million&nbsp;
views per minute. According to TikTok themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:31.560
25% of these views go to American creators which&nbsp;
translates to 167 million views per minute. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:39.300
the same as 87 trillion views per year. I had to&nbsp;
double check that number like 7 times because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:46.740
just seemed so wrong but that’s the number, 87&nbsp;
trillion views. Now, TikTok doesn’t pay very much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:53.040
They only pay about 2 to 4 cents per thousand&nbsp;
views. So, that 87 trillion views translates to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:59.640
just $1.75 billion. But, we all know that the&nbsp;
real money on TikTok isn’t with TikTok ads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:05.940
it’s with sponsorships and brand deals. For&nbsp;
creators, TikTok ad revenue is likely at most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:11.580
5% of their total TikTok revenue meaning that&nbsp;
American creators alone are actually pulling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:17.220
in closer to $30 to $40 billion through TikTok.&nbsp;
And if companies are paying creators this much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.320
they’re likely pulling a 3 to 4 times&nbsp;
that themselves. So, we’re talking about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:28.140
$100 billion economy here, the vast majority of&nbsp;
which doesn’t even go to TikTok. For perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:34.800
if TikTok US was a country, it would be rank&nbsp;
63 on the GDP list. And all of this is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:40.020
possible because ByteDance is subsidizing&nbsp;
the platform. So, who’s the one who really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:47.100
needs TikTok to survive. ByteDance or this $100&nbsp;
billion industry? Clearly, it’s the latter, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:52.260
TikTok’s influence on the American economy goes&nbsp;
much deeper than just creators and advertisers.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.600
PHASE 2 - WIN INFLUENCE:&nbsp;

00:05:54.600 --> 00:06:05.340
TikTok has clearly built a thriving social media&nbsp;
economy in the US but as we previously touched,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:11.160
this primarily consists of small businesses and&nbsp;
individual creators. The Apples and Coca Colas of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.500
the world don’t really want to get involved.&nbsp;
On one hand, this is a good thing. ByteDance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.720
can argue that a ban on TikTok would simply harm&nbsp;
small business owners like this guy. I mean, do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:27.180
you really wanna screw up this guy's business? Of&nbsp;
course not. But sympathy only goes so far. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:32.460
really want congress to be on your side, you need&nbsp;
money. Now, the CC I mean ByteDance has plenty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.680
cash but there’s no chance that they could just&nbsp;
directly lobby Congress. If some congressman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:42.613
accepts lobbying dollars from ByteDance, they’re&nbsp;
literally advertising that they don’t want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.613 --> 00:06:49.260
reelected so that’s not gonna work. But, what if&nbsp;
you introduced a proxy. A middle man that could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.900
effectively translate cash to political influence.&nbsp;
Hmm, where could you possibly find that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:59.940
Oh yeah, the entirety of the big tech industry.&nbsp;
Wasn’t there that one tech company that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:05.760
willing to buy TikTok? I think they’re name was&nbsp;
Oracle, why not just partner with them? Oh wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:11.040
that’s exactly what they’re doing. In mid 2022,&nbsp;
TikTok agreed to store all of their US data on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.180
Oracle’s databases and that all traffic&nbsp;
would be routed through Oracle servers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.620
Don’t mistake this for TikTok actually giving&nbsp;
up control though. They’re going to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.180
storing backups themselves because they want to&nbsp;
ensure that they don’t lose access to your data,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.860
I mean, they don’t want you to lose access&nbsp;
to your data. It’s not just Oracle that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.880
partnering with either. They’ve purchased $800&nbsp;
million worth of cloud services from Google,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:38.940
they’ve partnered with Microsoft on an AI project,&nbsp;
and they’re integrating Shopify into TikTok. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.440
partnerships accomplish two goals for TikTok.&nbsp;
For one, these companies can vouch for TikTok&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.760
that they are indeed properly storing their&nbsp;
data and not using it for nefarious purposes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:53.160
at least not the data that’s stored on Oracle&nbsp;
servers in America. And two, these companies can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:58.980
work their connections in Congress and persuade&nbsp;
them to go easy on TikTok because well, TikTok is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:05.040
a big partner/customer for them. This in itself is&nbsp;
a pretty strong case for TikTok but it gets even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:10.260
better. TikTok can also argue that they’re&nbsp;
supporting big American businesses and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:15.720
pushing forward AI development in conjunction with&nbsp;
Microsoft. In reality, all they’re doing is buying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:21.300
out the support of these big tech companies. But&nbsp;
buying out businesses is just phase 2 of TikTok’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:27.000
grand plan. The real power comes from buying out&nbsp;
people which is exactly what they’re doing now.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:36.420
PHASE 3 - SELL OUTS:
By now, I’m sure you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:41.760
all well aware of the big tech layoffs. Everyone&nbsp;
from Google and Facebook to Microsoft and Amazon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:46.620
is laying off tens of thousands of people.&nbsp;
This is precisely what ByteDance is doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:52.860
as well. They’re also laying off thousands of&nbsp;
people but there’s a caveat. Virtually all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:58.200
ByteDance’s layoffs are concentrated in China.&nbsp;
In the meantime, they’re not only maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:03.960
headcount in America but they’re aggressively&nbsp;
expanding headcount. In fact, they currently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:09.960
have over 3,400 positions open most of which&nbsp;
are in the US. Now, you might be wondering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:16.080
what type of person would take such a big risk and&nbsp;
join such a sketchy company. Well, the answer is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:22.380
virtually everyone given the right compensation.&nbsp;
And let’s just say, TikTok is hitting compensation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:28.440
out of the park. Take this data engineer position&nbsp;
for example. There’s nothing especially noteworthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:34.260
about this position. It’s not a director position&nbsp;
or a VP position or even a manager position. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.700
qualifications aren’t that crazy either. They’re&nbsp;
just looking for 1 year of experience in these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:44.700
basic areas. By all accounts, this is regular&nbsp;
old entry level position. That is until you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:52.020
look at the compensation. Up to a $250,000 base.&nbsp;
When you throw in stock compensation and bonuses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:58.200
you’re easily looking at $300 to $400,000 for an&nbsp;
entry level data engineer position. Let’s take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:03.060
look at another one. This one is a Data Scientist&nbsp;
position looking for just 3 years of experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:08.220
For some context, let’s take a look at what&nbsp;
Google pays. For an entry level Data Scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:15.360
they pay $180,000. That’s already a stellar salary&nbsp;
and one of the best offers you can get. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:21.660
TikTok’s minimum base itself is larger than&nbsp;
Google's total comp. Again, if you throw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:27.240
in stock and bonus, you’re looking at $300 to&nbsp;
$350 for an entry level position. Hearing that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:32.340
I’m sure you’re wondering what TikTok pays for&nbsp;
an actual senior position. Well, here’s a senior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:38.100
product manager position. TikTok is offering&nbsp;
a base of up to $400,000. For perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:44.700
even Google’s directors fall $90,000 short of that&nbsp;
base. Also, TikTok isn’t just posting these random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:50.520
ranges. They’re actually following through with&nbsp;
offers. This guy for example was already making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:57.600
$345 at Facebook. TikTok, however, came in with&nbsp;
an` offer for $525. Now, if we’re being real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.620
there’s no way that TikTok actually values&nbsp;
this person’s work contributions at over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:07.140
half a million per year. They can literally pay&nbsp;
someone in China a tenth of the salary and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:12.720
them to work 9 to 9 six days a week. But instead,&nbsp;
TikTok is actively laying people off in China and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:18.420
replacing them with American counterparts that&nbsp;
are 5 to 10 times as expensive. Why you ask? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:24.060
it all has to do with optics. That guy isn’t worth&nbsp;
anywhere near half a million per year for TikTok&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:29.220
in terms of work input, but that guy is worth half&nbsp;
a million per year for TikTok in terms of optics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:34.380
TikTok already has nearly 7,000 employees&nbsp;
in the US and at the current rate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:39.780
this will grow to tens of thousands in no time.&nbsp;
This way, when Congress finally comes around to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:45.360
taking action on a ban in 6 or 12 months,&nbsp;
TikTok can confidently tell Congress. Yo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:50.040
we’re pro American. We’re literally employing&nbsp;
tens of thousands of Americans at salaries that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:55.740
are 1.5 to 2 times what even Google offers. Do&nbsp;
you really wanna pull the cord this operation?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.740 --> 00:12:01.860
And that right there is TikTok’s Trump card.&nbsp;
Congress might be able to overlook a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:08.160
teens and their little influencer businesses. But,&nbsp;
what they can’t overlook is tens of thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:15.540
real tech jobs going to Americans. And that&nbsp;
is why TikTok will never be banned. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:20.940
TikTok has played their cards really well&nbsp;
and they aren’t going anywhere anytime soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:25.500
But, the same can’t be said about short form&nbsp;
content. Check out this video to learn more.

